{
  "_comment": "Plan §0, B2 final round 4. Each case's `facts` are what real git leaves behind for that flow: test/repos.reach.test.ts builds the flow, compares the engine's facts with them, runs `expect.command` for real and runs a plain `git push` to confirm what is a destination. tests/actions.rs mints from the same literal. `expect` is what the local branch `feat` may open, and `copy` is its refusal or, with `command`, what follows `git -C <repo> push`. When a pushRemote or pushDefault selects another remote, a branch's upstream is not its destination, whatever its name: the same-name-at-tip rule decides the links, on the selected remote. With no such selection, an upstream of the branch's own name is its destination, and one named differently is only when `pushesToUpstream` holds. Otherwise that upstream is only where the branch started: the same-name-at-tip rule decides the links, and Copy names the branch's own name with no -u. With two or more remotes and no selection, such a branch's Copy names `origin` when that is one of them, and otherwise has no remote to name and refuses `ambiguous`.",
